ry":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years, same as October to November. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 37% of normal in September to October and 182% in May to June. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 42% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, and grid 13976 bottomed out at 49%.</p>"}
